      SOFTWARE, and the SOFTWARE may not be run concurrently (i.e., it may
      only be launched on one computer at a time). Client may convert a Named
      User License to a Computer-Based License by paying the applicable fees
      and amending Client's Purchase Agreement. In the case of a Named User
      License, if any of the computers on which the SOFTWARE may be installed
      is a laptop, notebook or similar portable computer, or, in the case of a
      computer-based license, if the single computer is a laptop, notebook or
      similar portable computer, you may use the SOFTWARE on the portable
      computer while temporarily away from your workplace for the same purpose
      permitted by this Agreement as you normally use the SOFTWARE on the
      portable computer while in your workplace.

   B. Computer-Based License If the Client has acquired a Computer-Based
      License or converted a Named User License to a Computer-Based License as
